<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raghudev Narayan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1603</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raghudev Narayan was the son of the Koch general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilarai">Chilarai</a> and the first ruler of Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajo">Hajo</a>, the eastern part of the Koch kingdom in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>. In 1581 his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara-narayan">Nara Narayan</a> gave him the lands east of the Sankosh river. He ruled from Hajo, where he rebuilt the Hayagriva Madhava temple in 1583, and he was a rival of the Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> line until his death in 1603.</p></div>
